# An upper bound of a b, for every pair of finite numbers (milestone2.md, "Rounding a product down
# and up"): RU(a b) when a b = 0 or |a b| >= P = 2^(2p-1) eta; below it, RU(a b) or the number of
# the format after it. The listing of mul_down_1 on the other side; like it, evaluated with the
# FMA of two_prod only, and not constexpr in this milestone. An infinite or NaN operand gives the
# product of IEEE 754.
kernel:        mul_up_1
input:         a
input:         b
output:        r
value:         a*b
ensures:       bound r above steps=1
ensures:       rounded r up when=product_large
min_precision: 2
source:        two_prod and the sign of its error term (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   r is p or succ(p), chosen by select, and succ(-inf) is finite; the bound and rounded claims state the output for infinite and NaN operands

(p, e) = two_prod(a, b)
ap     = abs(p)
bd     = lt(ap, const up(eta/(2*u^2)))
ez     = eq(e, 0)
un     = and(bd, ez)
n      = lt(0, e)
su     = or(n, un)
sp     = succ(p)
v      = select(su, sp, p)
za     = eq(a, 0)
zb     = eq(b, 0)
zz     = or(za, zb)
r      = select(zz, p, v)
